  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit, FYE 9/30/2023. Governmental lines from Exhibit E (Totals 2023 column, p4); Taxes 159,940 split into property 60,718 / motor vehicle 10,665 / sales 88,557 and Intergovernmental revenues 67,450 split into highway allocation, motor vehicle fees, homestead allocation and other, using the Schedule 1 Totals 2023 column (p8), each adding up exactly; municipal equalization aid 0. Sale of properties 11,381 is printed under other financing sources -> other_financing. Fund balances 538,880 -> 790,399. Cash = cash in bank + cash with county treasurer from the governmental funds statement (p3; 2022 comparative column for the beginning); CDs as investments. Business-type (single proprietary column) lines from Exhibit H (p6), which ties exactly to the Statement of Activities (expenses 228,937, charges 151,136, investment earnings 2,602, transfers 144,743 / (200), net position 481,536 -> 550,880, p2). Contract services 0 omitted. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) because the governmental funds statement (790,399) does not equal governmental activities (capital assets, long-term debt); business-type cash in bank and county treasurer are 0. Detail: Schedule 1 (per fund, p8) and Schedule 3 (proprietary, Actual column, p10); Schedule 2 (p9) is a combined budget summary (receipts 945,364 vs budget 421,055; disbursements 691,243 vs budget 1,168,500) with no line items, not recorded. Proprietary cash flow statement (p7) not recorded (cash basis). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
